WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.714
Welcome. This class treats a model
repository as supply-chain input,

2
00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:11.429
not as a harmless collection of weights.
You will design

3
00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:17.143
a quarantine boundary, distinguish what
each verification signal proves, inspect

4
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:22.857
executable and parser surfaces before
loading, give every transformation a

5
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:28.571
new identity, and promote only a complete
immutable bundle with

6
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:34.286
a tested revocation path. We will use
synthetic manifests. No

7
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:40.000
real model download or execution is
required.

8
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.154
Acquire the exact pinned revision into a
non-serving, non-production quarantine.

9
00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:52.308
The environment has no learner data, no
production credentials, minimal

10
00:00:52.308 --> 00:00:58.462
network access, bounded storage and
compute, and an operator-approved

11
00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:04.615
destination. Preserve repository metadata
and original filenames. Do not enable

12
00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:10.769
remote code, plugins, post-install hooks,
or model loading merely to

13
00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:16.923
discover package contents. Before
transformation, record the authoritative

14
00:01:16.923 --> 00:01:23.077
source URL, immutable revision, retrieval
time, transfer mechanism, expected

15
00:01:23.077 --> 00:01:29.231
manifest, observed files, sizes, and
cryptographic digests. Compare expected

16
00:01:29.231 --> 00:01:35.385
and observed inventory. A mutable branch,
latest tag, cache entry,

17
00:01:35.385 --> 00:01:41.538
or friendly model name must never silently
replace the approved

18
00:01:41.538 --> 00:01:47.692
candidate. Quarantine is enforced
isolation plus policy. A folder called

19
00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:53.846
quarantine that shares production
credentials, runtime, caches, or network

20
00:01:53.846 --> 00:02:00.000
authority is not a trust boundary.

21
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.556
Consider a synthetic manifest expecting
two weight shards, one tokenizer,

22
00:02:05.556 --> 00:02:11.111
one configuration file, and one license
notice. The observed archive

23
00:02:11.111 --> 00:02:16.667
also contains an installer and a symbolic
link that points

24
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:22.222
outside the extraction root. A
filename-based check might accept the

25
00:02:22.222 --> 00:02:27.778
familiar shards and ignore the extras. A
safe acquisition records

26
00:02:27.778 --> 00:02:33.333
the full observed inventory, blocks
extraction traversal, marks the unexpected

27
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:38.889
executable surface, and holds the
candidate. The operator does not

28
00:02:38.889 --> 00:02:44.444
load the model to see whether it works.
The mismatch

29
00:02:44.444 --> 00:02:50.000
itself is enough to prevent promotion
while evidence is preserved.

30
00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.625
Verification signals answer different
questions. A cryptographic digest shows

31
00:02:55.625 --> 00:03:01.250
whether bytes match an expected digest. It
does not identify

32
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:06.875
a trustworthy publisher or prove safety. A
verified signature can

33
00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:12.500
bind signed material to an identity under
a trust policy.

34
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:18.125
It does not prove that the signer created
a safe

35
00:03:18.125 --> 00:03:23.750
or suitable model. Provenance can describe
where and how an

36
00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:29.375
artifact was produced, but the record must
be authenticated and

37
00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:35.000
compared with expected builder, source,
inputs, and process. Scanners can

38
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:40.625
report known malware, secrets, vulnerable
dependencies, suspicious files, or

39
00:03:40.625 --> 00:03:46.250
patterns within their configured coverage.
A clean result means no

40
00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:51.875
covered issue was reported, not that risk
is absent. A

41
00:03:51.875 --> 00:03:57.500
software bill of materials inventories
components and relationships. It does

42
00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:03.125
not prove correct licensing, secure
execution, model quality, or complete

43
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:08.750
behavior. Combine these signals with
license review, sandbox inspection,

44
00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:14.375
compatibility tests, evaluation, and human
decisions. Never collapse them into

45
00:04:14.375 --> 00:04:20.000
one green trust badge.

46
00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:26.667
Checkpoint. A candidate's digest matches
the expected value. What exactly

47
00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:33.333
has been established, and name two
important claims that still

48
00:04:33.333 --> 00:04:40.000
need different evidence.

49
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:00.714
The matching digest establishes byte
equality with the expected digest.

50
00:06:00.714 --> 00:06:06.429
It does not tell you who should have
published those

51
00:06:06.429 --> 00:06:12.143
bytes, how they were built, whether the
terms allow your

52
00:06:12.143 --> 00:06:17.857
use, whether loading is safe, or whether
model behavior meets

53
00:06:17.857 --> 00:06:23.571
requirements. If your answer used the word
trusted without naming

54
00:06:23.571 --> 00:06:29.286
the trust policy and other evidence,
narrow the claim and

55
00:06:29.286 --> 00:06:35.000
identify the next gate.

56
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:41.429
Inspect the complete executable and parser
surface before model loading.

57
00:06:41.429 --> 00:06:47.857
Repositories can contain serialized
objects, Python modules, native

58
00:06:47.857 --> 00:06:54.286
extensions, build scripts, package
metadata, custom operators, tokenizer

59
00:06:54.286 --> 00:07:00.714
code, templates, conversion tools, and
runtime plugins. PyTorch warns not

60
00:07:00.714 --> 00:07:07.143
to load data from an untrusted source
because loading can

61
00:07:07.143 --> 00:07:13.571
use unpickling. Restricted weight-only
modes narrow some exposure but do

62
00:07:13.571 --> 00:07:20.000
not eliminate resource exhaustion or
memory-corruption risk. Prefer

63
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.429
non-executable tensor formats when the
chosen runtime supports them, but

64
00:07:26.429 --> 00:07:32.857
do not trust an extension alone. Inspect
archive traversal, symbolic

65
00:07:32.857 --> 00:07:39.286
links, oversized or malformed tensors,
unexpected files, dependency installers,

66
00:07:39.286 --> 00:07:45.714
custom-code flags, dynamic imports,
network calls, and conversion steps. Run

67
00:07:45.714 --> 00:07:52.143
any unavoidable parser or converter in a
disposable least-privileged sandbox

68
00:07:52.143 --> 00:07:58.571
with strict CPU, memory, storage, time,
and network limits. Capture

69
00:07:58.571 --> 00:08:05.000
the result without granting the candidate
production authority.

70
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Treat every material transformation as a
new artifact identity. Conversion,

71
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:19.000
merging, pruning, quantization, sharding,
repackaging, or changing a tokenizer or

72
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:26.000
template can alter bytes, behavior,
dependencies, compatibility, and

73
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.000
obligations. Record input digests, tool
and dependency versions, configuration,

74
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:40.000
command or workflow, isolated environment,
output inventory and digests, operator

75
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:47.000
or automation identity, and the resulting
evaluation target. Link the

76
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:54.000
output to inputs through authenticated
provenance and verification expectations.

77
00:08:54.000 --> 00:09:01.000
Repeat license, integrity, compatibility,
and evaluation gates for the transformed

78
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:08.000
candidate. Do not inherit approval merely
because the process began

79
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:15.000
with approved weights. The derived
artifact earns its own decision.

80
00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:21.538
Promote a complete immutable bundle, not a
convenient filename. The

81
00:09:21.538 --> 00:09:28.077
bundle identifies weights, tokenizer,
template, configuration, runtime,

82
00:09:28.077 --> 00:09:34.615
dependencies, and policy; records digests,
signatures or documented absence,

83
00:09:34.615 --> 00:09:41.154
provenance, scans, license disposition,
compatibility, evaluation target,

84
00:09:41.154 --> 00:09:47.692
reviewers, and expiry triggers; and moves
by digest into a

85
00:09:47.692 --> 00:09:54.231
read-only trusted store. Serving resolves
only the approved immutable identity.

86
00:09:54.231 --> 00:10:00.769
Fail closed when files, digests, signer
identity, provenance predicates, lineage,

87
00:10:00.769 --> 00:10:07.308
terms, dependency review, scans, or
sandbox checks violate policy. Preserve

88
00:10:07.308 --> 00:10:13.846
evidence, block serving, revoke the
candidate from controlled caches and

89
00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:20.385
mirrors, investigate affected
environments, and restore the last

90
00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:26.923
verified bundle. Rehearse that procedure
before release. Revocation is incomplete

91
00:10:26.923 --> 00:10:33.462
if one mutable alias, warm cache, or
disconnected site can

92
00:10:33.462 --> 00:10:40.000
continue serving the rejected bytes.

93
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:45.625
Now design the synthetic artifact
promotion packet. Define quarantine,

94
00:10:45.625 --> 00:10:51.250
immutable source and inventory, digest and
signature policy, provenance expectations,

95
00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:56.875
scanning, dependency inventory, and
executable-surface review. Add one

96
00:10:56.875 --> 00:11:02.500
quantization transformation with new input
and output identities. Write pass,

97
00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:08.125
hold, and fail-closed rules, including
unsafe deserialization and resource

98
00:11:08.125 --> 00:11:13.750
exhaustion. Finish with the
promoted-bundle manifest and a revocation

99
00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:19.375
procedure that restores the last verified
bundle without destroying investigation

100
00:11:19.375 --> 00:11:25.000
evidence.

101
00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:29.118
The fixed inventory contains
`fixtures/artifact.bin`, an empty inert

102
00:14:29.118 --> 00:14:33.235
file, and `fixtures/tokenizer.txt`, the
exact three bytes `abc`. The verifier

103
00:14:33.235 --> 00:14:37.353
first validates manifest structure,
trusted local fixture-policy expectations,

104
00:14:37.353 --> 00:14:41.471
safe paths, complete filesystem
enumeration, file sizes, SHA-256 digests,

105
00:14:41.471 --> 00:14:45.588
SBOM equality, executable-surface
declarations, signature disposition,

106
00:14:45.588 --> 00:14:49.706
provenance fields, and scan scope. The
starter's one deliberate defect

107
00:14:49.706 --> 00:14:53.824
occurs only at the final transition. It
compares the canonical

108
00:14:53.824 --> 00:14:57.941
verified inventory binding with the bundle
label `local-fixture-v1` instead of

109
00:14:57.941 --> 00:15:02.059
the manifest's exact
`promotion.inventoryBinding`. Repair only

110
00:15:02.059 --> 00:15:06.176
the marked expression in `verify.mjs`,
replacing `manifest.bundleId` with

111
00:15:06.176 --> 00:15:10.294
`manifest.promotion.inventoryBinding`. Do
not hardcode either fixture digest, bypass

112
00:15:10.294 --> 00:15:14.412
a failed gate, trust a filename as proof,
edit immutable

113
00:15:14.412 --> 00:15:18.529
tests, or reject every input. After
repair, the baseline exits

114
00:15:18.529 --> 00:15:22.647
0 and ends with `PROMOTION PASS
bundle=local-fixture-v1`. The independent

115
00:15:22.647 --> 00:15:26.765
same-length tamper variation changes `abc`
to `abd` while retaining size

116
00:15:26.765 --> 00:15:30.882
3 and leaving the expected manifest
unchanged. A second changed-input

117
00:15:30.882 --> 00:15:35.000
variation updates the copied test manifest
and inventory binding to

118
00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.118
that independently calculated digest. It
passes the narrow local fixture

119
00:15:39.118 --> 00:15:43.235
policy, demonstrating that the learner did
not substitute a hardcoded

120
00:15:43.235 --> 00:15:47.353
allowlist of the original hashes. This
controlled test does not

121
00:15:47.353 --> 00:15:51.471
imply that an attacker-controlled
production manifest should be trusted.

122
00:15:51.471 --> 00:15:55.588
Node.js `fileURLToPath` converts
`import.meta.url` to a

123
00:15:55.588 --> 00:15:59.706
platform-appropriate filesystem path,
`webcrypto.subtle.digest('SHA-256',

124
00:15:59.706 --> 00:16:03.824
bytes)` computes the digest,
`path.relative` supports containment

125
00:16:03.824 --> 00:16:07.941
checks, and `fsPromises.lstat` identifies
symbolic links. The reference uses an

126
00:16:07.941 --> 00:16:12.059
explicit workspace argument as-is. Its
default is the parent of

127
00:16:12.059 --> 00:16:16.176
its own `reference` directory, correcting
the earlier defect that moved

128
00:16:16.176 --> 00:16:20.294
every explicit workspace to its parent.
Use this rubric: complete

129
00:16:20.294 --> 00:16:24.412
work changes only the marked binding
expression, passes all immutable

130
00:16:24.412 --> 00:16:28.529
tests, accepts the independently changed
trusted fixture, rejects same-length

131
00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:32.647
tampering and every negative case,
preserves exact output and exit

132
00:16:32.647 --> 00:16:36.765
behavior, and explains why digest success
is narrower than provenance

133
00:16:36.765 --> 00:16:40.882
or safety. A deny-all implementation,
hardcoded fixture-hash check, edited test,

134
00:16:40.882 --> 00:16:45.000
skipped enumeration, or fabricated
signature result does not pass.

135
00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.350
Meta Llama, Qwen, DeepSeek, Mistral, and
Microsoft Phi are examples

136
00:16:49.350 --> 00:16:53.700
of distinct model-family ecosystems. They
are not one shared runtime,

137
00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:58.050
format, tokenizer, license, API,
capability set, or custom-code policy.

138
00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.400
Consult the documentation and release
evidence for the exact selected

139
00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:06.750
artifact and runtime rather than inferring
compatibility from a family

140
00:17:06.750 --> 00:17:11.100
name. The transferable procedure is
provider-neutral: pin the source,

141
00:17:11.100 --> 00:17:15.450
quarantine the complete package, enumerate
every artifact file, reject unsafe

142
00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:19.800
paths and executable surfaces, verify
bytes against independently trusted

143
00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:24.150
expectations, evaluate signatures and
provenance under policy, bind

144
00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:28.500
transformations to new identities, impose
resource limits, conduct runtime-specific

145
00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:32.850
evaluations, and promote an immutable
reviewed bundle. Keep four layers

146
00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:37.200
separate. A model family names related
model releases. An artifact

147
00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:41.550
is a specific set of bytes and metadata. A

148
00:17:41.550 --> 00:17:45.900
runtime loads or executes an artifact
under its own compatibility

149
00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:50.250
and security constraints. An API exposes
operations under a provider-specific

150
00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:54.600
contract. Evidence for one layer does not
automatically approve another.

151
00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:58.950
The lab has no integration with Meta,
Qwen, DeepSeek, Mistral,

152
00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:03.300
Phi, Hugging Face, PyTorch, a model
runtime, or a live

153
00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:07.650
endpoint. Provider names establish
transfer scope only. No common capability,

154
00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:12.000
format support, or deployment approval is
asserted.

155
00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:17.000
Begin the knowledge check when you can
defend quarantine, bound

156
00:18:17.000 --> 00:18:22.000
every verification claim, identify
executable loading risk, treat

157
00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:27.000
transformations as new artifacts, explain
scanner limits, and execute a

158
00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:32.000
fail-closed mismatch response. The
assessment starts only when you choose

159
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:37.000
Begin knowledge check.

160
00:18:37.000 --> 00:18:42.000
Keep one rule: inspect before execution,
prove each claim with

161
00:18:42.000 --> 00:18:47.000
the right evidence, and promote only an
immutable bundle you

162
00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:52.000
already know how to revoke and replace.
